_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 15
---
order: 15
---
short_label: VI.15
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: In equal triangles which have one angle equal to one angle the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional; and those triangles which have one angle equal to one angle, and in which the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional, are equal.
----
proof:

Let {ABC|ABCt} and {ADE|ADEt} be equal triangles having one angle equal to one angle, namely the angle {BAC|angBAC} equal to the angle {DAE|angDAE}.

I say that in the triangles {ABC|ABCt} and {ADE|ADEt} the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional, that is to say, that {CA|AC} is to {AD} as {EA|AE} is to {AB}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="270" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VI.15 diagram" src="propVI15.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Euclid places the triangles vertex to vertex (CA in a straight line
    // with AD, so EA with AB), joins BD, and compares each triangle with ABD
    // (V.7, VI.1, V.11; the converse by VI.1, V.11, V.9).
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws both triangles (random faces) and BD. The proof
    // also names the sides about the angle at A, the triangle ABD and the
    // two equal angles: all added transparent (;0;0;0 lines, ;0;0;0;0
    // polygons), so the resting figure is unchanged. The triangles' own
    // polygons have filled faces, which a highlight would raise over the
    // angle markers inside them (#140), so caption and prose refs to the
    // triangles go to the faceless twins ABCt / ADEt via display overrides.
    // BD is declared B→D and strokes from B when joined, so no twin.
    //
    // Markers: BAC and DAE are vertical angles at A (equal, one colour),
    // pinned at 22 so the same-vertex stepping does not put them on
    // different rings. Neither is a right angle. Hidden at rest.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C free and D a
    // lineSlider on AC — all givens on slide 1. E is derived and listed per
    // slide; nothing to defer. The converse re-joins BD ("If BD is again
    // joined"), so BD and ABD are dropped while the converse is set out.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C","D","E","ABC","ADE","ABCt","ADEt",
                 "AB","AC","AD","AE","angBAC","angDAE"];
    var JOIN  = GIVEN.concat(["BD"]);
    var ALL   = JOIN.concat(["ABD"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VI.15",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;140,110",
            "B;point;free;80,30",
            "C;point;free;30,200",
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;black;random",
            "D;point;lineSlider;A,C,200,50",
            "E';point;extend;B,A,B,A;0;0",
            "E;point;proportion;A,D,A,C,A,B,A,E'",
            "ADE;polygon;triangle;A,D,E;0;0;black;random",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D",
            // Highlight targets, all transparent.
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0;0",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C;0;0;0",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D;0;0;0",
            "AE;line;connect;A,E;0;0;0",
            "ABCt;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;0;0",
            "ADEt;polygon;triangle;A,D,E;0;0;0;0",
            "ABD;polygon;triangle;A,B,D;0;0;0;0",
            "angBAC;sector;angleMarker;A,B,C,22;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angDAE;sector;angleMarker;A,D,E,22;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8"
        ],
        slides: [
            { text: "“In equal triangles which have one angle equal to one angle”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt","angBAC","angDAE"] },
            { text: "“the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional;”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC","AD","AE","AB"] },
            { text: "“and those triangles which have one angle equal to one angle,”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt","angBAC","angDAE"] },
            { text: "“and in which the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional, are equal.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC","AD","AE","AB","ABCt","ADEt"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.15" }] },
            { text: "Let {ABC|ABCt} and {ADE|ADEt} be equal triangles having one angle equal to one angle,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt"] },
            { text: "namely the angle {BAC|angBAC} equal to the angle {DAE|angDAE}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["angBAC","angDAE"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angBAC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angDAE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "I say that in the triangles {ABC|ABCt} and {ADE|ADEt} the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt"] },
            { text: "that is to say, that {CA|AC} is to {AD} as {EA|AE} is to {AB}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC","AD","AE","AB"] },
            { text: "Place them so that {CA|AC} is in a straight line with {AD}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC","AD"] },
            { text: "Therefore {EA|AE} is also in a straight line with {AB}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AE","AB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EA in a straight line with AB", ref: "I.14" }] },
            { text: "Join {BD}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["BD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "BD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Since then the triangle {ABC|ABCt} equals the triangle {ADE|ADEt}, and {ABD} is another triangle,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt","ABD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "ABD", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the triangle {ABC|ABCt} is to the triangle {ABD} as the triangle {ADE|ADEt} is to the triangle {ABD}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt","ABD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "equals have the same ratio to the same", ref: "V.7" }] },
            { text: "But {ABC|ABCt} is to {ABD} as {AC} is to {AD},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ABD","AC","AD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "triangles under the same height are as their bases", ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "and {ADE|ADEt} is to {ABD} as {AE} is to {AB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ADEt","ABD","AE","AB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "Therefore also {AC} is to {AD} as {AE} is to {AB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","AD","AE","AB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "ratios the same as the same ratio", ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "Therefore in the triangles {ABC|ABCt} and {ADE|ADEt} the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt","AC","AD","AE","AB"] },
            { text: "Next, let the sides of the triangles {ABC|ABCt} and {ADE|ADEt} be reciprocally proportional,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt"] },
            { text: "that is to say, let {AE} be to {AB} as {CA|AC} is to {AD}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AE","AB","AC","AD"] },
            { text: "I say that the triangle {ABC|ABCt} equals the triangle {ADE|ADEt}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt"] },
            { text: "If {BD} is again joined, since {AC} is to {AD} as {AE} is to {AB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BD","AC","AD","AE","AB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "BD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "while {AC} is to {AD} as the triangle {ABC|ABCt} is to the triangle {ABD},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","AD","ABCt","ABD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "triangles under the same height are as their bases", ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "and {AE} is to {AB} as the triangle {ADE|ADEt} is to the triangle {ABD},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AE","AB","ADEt","ABD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "therefore the triangle {ABC|ABCt} is to the triangle {ABD} as the triangle {ADE|ADEt} is to the triangle {ABD}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt","ABD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "ratios the same as the same ratio", ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "Therefore each of the triangles {ABC|ABCt} and {ADE|ADEt} has the same ratio to {ABD}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt","ABD"] },
            { text: "Therefore the triangle {ABC|ABCt} equals the triangle {ADE|ADEt}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "magnitudes with the same ratio to the same are equal", ref: "V.9" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, in equal triangles which have one angle equal to one angle",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt","angBAC","angDAE"] },
            { text: "the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional;",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","AD","AE","AB"] },
            { text: "and those triangles which have one angle equal to one angle,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCt","ADEt","angBAC","angDAE"] },
            { text: "and in which the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional, are equal.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","AD","AE","AB","ABCt","ADEt"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "VI.15") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.14":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI14/",
        "V.7":      "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV7/",
        "V.9":      "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV9/",
        "V.11":     "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV11/",
        "VI.1":     "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Place them so that {CA|AC} is in a straight line with {AD}. Therefore {EA|AE} is also in a straight line with {AB}. [!just I.14]

Join {BD}.

Since then the triangle {ABC|ABCt} equals the triangle {ADE|ADEt}, and {ABD} is another triangle, therefore the triangle {ABC|ABCt} is to the triangle {ABD} as the triangle {ADE|ADEt} is to the triangle {ABD}. [!just V.7]

But {ABC|ABCt} is to {ABD} as {AC} is to {AD}, and {ADE|ADEt} is to {ABD} as {AE} is to {AB}. [!just VI.1]

Therefore also {AC} is to {AD} as {AE} is to {AB}. [!just V.11]

Therefore in the triangles {ABC|ABCt} and {ADE|ADEt} the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional.

<hr width="50%">

Next, let the sides of the triangles {ABC|ABCt} and {ADE|ADEt} be reciprocally proportional, that is to say, let {AE} be to {AB} as {CA|AC} is to {AD}.

I say that the triangle {ABC|ABCt} equals the triangle {ADE|ADEt}.

If {BD} is again joined, since {AC} is to {AD} as {AE} is to {AB}, while {AC} is to {AD} as the triangle {ABC|ABCt} is to the triangle {ABD}, and {AE} is to {AB} as the triangle {ADE|ADEt} is to the triangle {ABD}, therefore the triangle {ABC|ABCt} is to the triangle {ABD} as the triangle {ADE|ADEt} is to the triangle {ABD}. [!just VI.1; V.11]

Therefore each of the triangles {ABC|ABCt} and {ADE|ADEt} has the same ratio to {ABD}.

Therefore the triangle {ABC|ABCt} equals the triangle {ADE|ADEt}. [!just V.9]

Therefore, *in equal triangles which have one angle equal to one angle the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional; and those triangles which have one angle equal to one angle, and in which the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional, are equal.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide: This proposition is used in the proof of proposition @VI.19.
